### Rotating Card (Hover Effect)

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows how to create a card that flips (rotates) when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    margin:0;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container (perspective) ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card itself (front + back) ---------- */
.card {
    width:300px;
    height:200px;
    position:relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;/* Smooth rotation */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front side ---------- */
.card .front,
.card .back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;     /* Hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:10px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.card .front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card .front h2 {
    margin:0 0 10px;
    font-size:1.5rem;
    color:#333;
}

.card .front p {
    margin:0;
    color:#666;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Back side ---------- */
.card .back {
    background:#4a90e2;
    color:#fff;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* Start rotated so it's hidden */
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    font-size:1.2rem;
}

/* ---------- 6️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);       /* Flip the card on hover */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="front">
            <h2>Front Title</h2>
            <p>This is the front side of the card.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="back">
            Back Side Content
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | Basic page styling | Centers the card on the screen. |
| **2** | `perspective` on wrapper | Creates a 3D space so the rotation looks realistic. |
| **3** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Allows child elements to maintain their 3D position. |
| **4** | `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each side when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| **5** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on back | Positions the back side initially hidden. |
| **6** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Flips the whole card when the mouse hovers over it. |

#### Customization tips

- **Change rotation axis**: Replace `rotateY` with `rotateX` for a vertical flip, or combine both for a 3D twist.
- **Add more sides**: Duplicate the `.front` and `.back` blocks, rotate them appropriately, and adjust the card’s `transform` on hover.
- **Add content**: Put images, icons, or other elements inside the `.front` or `.back` divs.
- **Adjust timing**: Change `0.6s` to a faster or slower duration, or use `cubic-bezier` for custom easing.

Enjoy experimenting with this rotating card!
